# context_label (Data Source)

Generates a label string from the provider context. Supports two modes: **delimited** (joins property values with a
delimiter) and **templated** (uses a Go template string like `{{"{{"}}.namespace{{"}}"}}/{{"{{"}}.environment{{"}}"}}/{{"{{"}}.name{{"}}"}}`). Override
context values per label, enforce max length, and control character replacement.

## Example Usage (Delimited)

In delimited mode, property values are joined using the provider's delimiter (or a per-label override) in the order
specified by `property_order`.

{{ tffile "examples/data-sources/label_delimited/data-source.tf" }}

The output will be:

```
rendered = "cp~plat~dev~ue1~example"
```

## Example Usage (Templated)

In templated mode, a Go template string is used to format the label. Context values are available as template variables.
This is useful when specific resources need names that break the pattern defined more globally.

{{ tffile "examples/data-sources/label_templated/data-source.tf" }}

The output will be:

```
rendered = "cp/plat/dev/example"
```

